          "java",
          "// 1. Depend on abstractions, not concretions\n// 2. Inject all collaborators through constructors\n// 3. Make dependencies explicit and required\n// 4. Keep the composition root (wiring) separate from business logic\n// 5. Use interfaces for anything that might have multiple implementations\n\n// Good: focused, testable, clear dependencies\npublic class InvoiceGenerator {\n    private final InvoiceRepository repository;\n    private final TaxCalculator taxCalculator;\n    private final PdfRenderer renderer;\n\n    public InvoiceGenerator(InvoiceRepository repository,\n                            TaxCalculator taxCalculator,\n                            PdfRenderer renderer) {\n        this.repository = repository;\n        this.taxCalculator = taxCalculator;\n        this.renderer = renderer;\n    }\n}"
        ]
